- Line 218: `dictionary.Add(new ResourceIdentifier(property0.Name), JsonSerializer.Deserialize<UserAssignedIdentity>(property0.Value.GetRawText()));`

Replace them as follows:

**Line 31** - The `ManagedServiceIdentityTypeConverter.Write` method writes `writer.WritePropertyName("type"); writer.WriteStringValue(model.ToString());`. So replace:
```csharp
JsonSerializer.Serialize(writer, ManagedServiceIdentityType, jOptions);
```
with:
```csharp
writer.WritePropertyName("type"u8);
writer.WriteStringValue(ManagedServiceIdentityType.ToString());
```

**Line 49** - `UserAssignedIdentity` implements `IJsonModel<UserAssignedIdentity>`. Replace:
```csharp
JsonSerializer.Serialize(writer, item.Value, jOptions);
```
with:
```csharp
if (item.Value is null)
{
    writer.WriteNullValue();
}
else
{
    ((IJsonModel<UserAssignedIdentity>)item.Value).Write(writer, options);
}
```
Note: `options` is the `ModelReaderWriterOptions` parameter available in the method scope.

**Line 206** - The converter reads `{"type": "value"}` and returns `new ManagedServiceIdentityType(value)`. The `property` here is a JsonProperty with name "type". Replace:
```csharp
type = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<ManagedServiceIdentityType>($"{{{property}}}");
